# Analects Book 5 (公冶長) — draft. One unit per stretch of text between Zhu Xi's commentary
# interruptions (39 units for 27 passages; Book 5 closes juan 3 of Zhu Xi's commentary but, being
# odd-numbered, has no 論語卷 running head in the lemma list). Token format as the pilot:
#   tokens separated by " | "; a token is  CHARS[PUNCT][=pinyin][/context gloss[//char gloss//char gloss]]
#   a leading "^" breaks the verse line before the token.
# Punctuation is editorial (the edition has none) and always trails the word before it.
# Pinyin defaults to the glossary's first reading; every polyphone states its reading here.
# Misprints corrected in the reading text (rule 5b; emend.json entries needed), the note opening
# with the print's reading:
#   unit 15 (5.9): the print has 宰子 for 宰予;  unit 22 (5.15): the print has 已 for 己 (行己).
# Glyphs kept as the edition prints them: 乗 (= 乘, 千乗), 賔 (= 賓), 産 (= 產), 髙 (= 高),
# 顔/顏 (both, as printed), 巳 (= 已, read yǐ, in 巳矣乎), 内 (= 內), 説 (= 悅, read yuè), 弑, 棁.
# 三已之 (5.18) is the real 已 'to dismiss', not a misprint.
# Quotation marks: a unit cannot open with 「 (punctuation trails a word), so the follow-up questions
# that open units 10, 11 and 26 are left unquoted in the Chinese; quotes balance within every unit.

