dict(pas="5.6", w="子/the Master | 曰：「/said | ^道=dào/the Way | 不/does not | 行，=xíng/go forward, prevail | ^乘=chéng/(I will) ride | 桴=fú/a raft | 浮=fú/(and) float out | 于/on | 海。=hǎi/the sea | ^從=cóng/following | 我/me | 者，/(the one who) | 其/surely, would it be | 由/Yóu | 與？」=yú/(question) | ^子路=zǐ lù/Zilu — the disciple Zhong You//Master//Lu (his courtesy name) | 聞/heard | 之/it | 喜。/(and) was glad | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | ^由/Yóu | 也/(pause) | 好=hào/loves | 勇/courage | 過/beyond | 我，/me | ^無/(but) has nothing | 所/(with) which | 取/to take | 材。」=cái/measure (= 裁 cái, 'to cut to fit')",
  l="The Master said: “The Way does not go forward —\nI will ride a raft and drift out on the sea.\nThe one to follow me — would it be Yóu?”\nZilu heard it and was glad.\nThe Master said: “Yóu loves courage beyond me,\nbut has nothing to take his measure by.”",
  i="The Master said: “The Way is getting nowhere. I shall take a raft and let the sea carry me — and if anyone comes with me, it will surely be Yóu.” Zilu heard this and was delighted. The Master said: “Yóu's love of daring outruns mine; but he has no means of weighing things up.”",
  n="由 Yóu is Zhong You 仲由, courtesy name Zilu 子路 (2.17). 乘 here is chéng, 'to ride, to board' (not shèng 'chariot'); 桴 fú is a raft (Zhu Xi: 筏也; He Yan's Ma Rong: bamboo or wood lashed together, the big ones called 筏 and the small 桴). 于 = 於. 從 Zhu Xi reads zòng, 'to follow in attendance' (從…去聲), a reading modern practice does not keep; we give cóng. 其…與 'would it be…?': 其 softens, and 與 is the question particle yú (Zhu Xi: 平聲). 好 is hào 'to love' (Zhu Xi: 去聲). The last word is the puzzle. Zhu Xi: 材 here is 裁 'to cut, to judge', the old graph borrowed (材與裁同，古字借用). He quotes Master Cheng: the sigh about the sea grieves that the world has no worthy ruler; Zilu was brave for what is right, so the Master said he would follow — all said in supposition; Zilu took it as real and was glad to be chosen, so the Master praised his courage and mocked his inability to weigh the principle of things and fit it to what is right. He Yan's Zheng Xuan reads it as a joke: Zilu missed the hidden meaning, so the Master teased him — 'there is nowhere to get timber for the raft'. Variant: He Yan's text reads 浮於海 and 其由也與."),
