dict(w="又/again | 問。/(he) asked | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | 由/Yóu | 也，/(pause: 'as for') | ^千乗=qiān shèng/a thousand chariots (乗 = 乘)//a thousand//war chariot (乗, the edition's form of 乘) | 之/'s | 國，/state | ^可/(he) could | 使/be set | 治=zhì/to manage | 其/its | 賦=fù/levies — the army raised from the fields | 也；/(assertion) | ^不/(I) do not | 知=zhī/know | 其/his | 仁/humaneness | 也。」/(assertion)",
  l="He asked again.\nThe Master said: “Yóu —\na state of a thousand chariots:\nhe could be set to manage its levies.\nI do not know about his humaneness.”",
  i="He asked again. The Master said: “Yóu could be put in charge of the levies of a state of a thousand chariots. Whether he is humane I cannot say.”",
  n="千乗 is the edition's form of 千乘 (1.5), 'a thousand chariots', the measure of a major state; 乗 is the same word, read shèng (Zhu Xi: 乘去聲). 由也 'as for Yóu': 也 after a name sets up the topic. 可使 'could be made to, could be employed to'. 賦 is a levy. Zhu Xi: here it means troops — in old times the army was raised by levy on the fields, so troops were called 賦, as in the Zuo zhuan's 悉索敝賦 'gather all our poor levies'; He Yan's Kong Anguo: the military levy. Zhu Xi: this is what can be seen of Zilu's talent; his humaneness cannot be known."),
dict(w="求/Qiu — Ran Qiu | 也/(pause) | 何如？=hé rú/what of (him) | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | 求/Qiu | 也，/(pause: 'as for') | ^千/a thousand | 室=shì/households' | 之/(of) | 邑，=yì/town | ^百乘=bǎi shèng/a hundred chariots//a hundred//war chariot | 之/'s | 家，/house | ^可/(he) could | 使/be set | 為=wéi/to act as | 之/its | 宰=zǎi/steward | 也；/(assertion) | ^不/(I) do not | 知=zhī/know | 其/his | 仁/humaneness | 也。」/(assertion)",
  l="“Qiu — what of him?”\nThe Master said: “Qiu —\na town of a thousand households,\na house of a hundred chariots:\nhe could be set to act as its steward.\nI do not know about his humaneness.”",
  i="“And Qiu?” The Master said: “Qiu could be made steward of a town of a thousand households, or of a house that musters a hundred chariots. Whether he is humane I cannot say.”",
  n="求 Qiu is Ran Qiu 冉求, courtesy name Ziyou 子有 — the 冉有 of 3.6, who served the Ji house. 千室之邑 'a town of a thousand households', which Zhu Xi calls a large town; 百乘之家 'a house of a hundred chariots' is the household of a minister or grandee (Zhu Xi: 卿大夫之家; He Yan's Kong Anguo: a feudal lord has a thousand chariots, a minister or grandee a hundred). 乘 is shèng. 為之宰 'act as its steward': 為 is wéi, and 之 'its' covers both the town and the house. 宰, Zhu Xi says, is the common title of a town's head and of a great house's chief retainer."),
dict(w="赤=chì/Chi — Gongxi Chi | 也/(pause) | 何如？=hé rú/what of (him) | ^子/the Master | 曰：「/said | 赤/Chi | 也，/(pause: 'as for') | ^束=shù/binding on | 帶=dài/(his) sash | 立/standing | 於/at | 朝，=cháo/court | ^可/(he) could | 使/be set | 與=yǔ/with | 賔=bīn/guests (賔, the edition's form of 賓) | 客=kè/(and) visitors | 言/to speak | 也；/(assertion) | ^不/(I) do not | 知=zhī/know | 其/his | 仁/humaneness | 也。」/(assertion)",
  l="“Chi — what of him?”\nThe Master said: “Chi —\nsash bound on, standing at court,\nhe could be set to speak with guests and visitors.\nI do not know about his humaneness.”",
  i="“And Chi?” The Master said: “Chi, in his court sash, standing in the hall, could be given the task of receiving envoys and guests. Whether he is humane I cannot say.”",
  n="赤 Chi is Gongxi Chi 公西赤, courtesy name Zihua 子華, a disciple (Zhu Xi; He Yan's Ma Rong). 束帶 'binding on the sash', in full court dress. 朝 is cháo, 'court' (Zhu Xi: 音潮), not zhāo 'morning'. 賔 is the edition's form of 賓 bīn; 賓客 are guests and visitors, here envoys from other states. 與 is yǔ, 'with'. Ma Rong: Chi had a fine bearing and could serve as the officer who receives envoys. The three answers have one shape: a talent the Master can vouch for, and humaneness he will not."),
