dict(pas="5.8", w="子/the Master | 謂/spoke to | 子貢/Zigong | 曰：「/saying | 女=rǔ/you | 與=yǔ/and | 回/Hui | 也，/(pause: 'as for') | 孰=shú/which | 愈？」=yù/is better",
  l="The Master said to Zigong: “You and Hui — which is the better?”",
  i="The Master said to Zigong: “Set yourself beside Hui: which of you comes out ahead?”",
  n="謂…曰 here is 'spoke to … saying', not 'said of' as in 5.1–5.2. 女 is rǔ, 'you' (Zhu Xi: 女音汝，下同 'and so below'); 與 is yǔ, 'and'. 回 Hui is Yan Hui 顏回 (2.9), the disciple the Master loved most. 孰 shú 'which (of the two)'; 愈 yù 'to surpass, be better' (Zhu Xi and He Yan's Kong Anguo: 勝也)."),
dict(w="對/(he) answered | 曰：「/saying | 賜/Ci | 也/(pause) | 何/how | 敢=gǎn/dare | 望=wàng/look toward | 回？/Hui | ^回/Hui | 也/(pause) | 聞/hears | 一/one | 以/and by it | 知=zhī/knows | 十；/ten | ^賜/Ci | 也/(pause) | 聞/hears | 一/one | 以/and by it | 知=zhī/knows | 二。」/two",
  l="He answered, saying: “How would Ci dare look toward Hui?\nHui hears one and by it knows ten;\nCi hears one and by it knows two.”",
  i="He answered: “How could I so much as set my sights on Hui? Hui learns one thing and from it works out ten; I learn one and get to two.”",
  n="Zigong calls himself by his personal name 賜, as is proper before his teacher. 望 is to gaze at from afar — to aspire to, hope to come level with. 以 joins the two verbs: 'hear one, and by it know ten'. Zhu Xi: one is the beginning of numbers and ten their end; two is one's counterpart. Yan Hui's clear and penetrating mind saw the end in the beginning; Zigong worked things out by inference, getting from this to that. The proofs, he says, are Hui's 'nothing in my words he does not delight in' (Book 11) and Zigong's 'told what has gone, he knows what is to come' (1.15)."),
